{"slug":"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/equilibrium/","source":"students/subjects/physics/mechanics/equilibrium.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Equilibrium of Forces | Physics Mechanics","description":"","subject":"physics","body":"<div class=\"max-w-6xl mx-auto\">\n        <nav class=\"mb-8\">\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700\">← Back to Mechanics</a>\n        </nav>\n\n        <div class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-8\">\n            <header class=\"mb-12\">\n                <h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Equilibrium of Forces</h1>\n                <p class=\"text-lg text-gray-600\">Understanding static and dynamic equilibrium in physical systems</p>\n            </header>\n\n            <div class=\"grid gap-8\">\n                <!-- Conditions for Equilibrium -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Conditions for Equilibrium</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Translational Equilibrium</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• ΣF = 0 (Net force is zero)</li>\n                                    <li>• ΣFx = 0 (x-direction)</li>\n                                    <li>• ΣFy = 0 (y-direction)</li>\n                                    <li>• No linear acceleration</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Rotational Equilibrium</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• Στ = 0 (Net torque is zero)</li>\n                                    <li>• Choose convenient pivot point</li>\n                                    <li>• Consider all forces' moments</li>\n                                    <li>• No angular acceleration</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Types of Equilibrium -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Types of Equilibrium</h2>\n                    <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6\">\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Stable Equilibrium</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• Returns to original position</li>\n                                <li>• Minimum potential energy</li>\n                                <li>• Example: Pendulum at rest</li>\n                                <li>• Self-correcting</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Unstable Equilibrium</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• Moves away from position</li>\n                                <li>• Maximum potential energy</li>\n                                <li>• Example: Pencil on point</li>\n                                <li>• Any disturbance critical</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Neutral Equilibrium</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• Stays in new position</li>\n                                <li>• Constant potential energy</li>\n                                <li>• Example: Ball on flat surface</li>\n                                <li>• No restoring force</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Free Body Diagrams -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Free Body Diagrams</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Key Components</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• Object as a point/extended body</li>\n                                    <li>• All external forces shown</li>\n                                    <li>• Force magnitude and direction</li>\n                                    <li>• Coordinate system</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Common Forces</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• Weight (mg)</li>\n                                    <li>• Normal force (N)</li>\n                                    <li>• Tension (T)</li>\n                                    <li>• Friction (f)</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Problem-Solving Strategy -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Problem-Solving Strategy</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <ol class=\"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700\">\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-1\">Draw Free Body Diagram</p>\n                                <p class=\"text-sm\">Show all forces acting on the object</p>\n                            </li>\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-1\">Choose Coordinate System</p>\n                                <p class=\"text-sm\">Select convenient axes for analysis</p>\n                            </li>\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-1\">Apply Equilibrium Conditions</p>\n                                <p class=\"text-sm\">Write equations for forces and torques</p>\n                            </li>\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-1\">Solve Equations</p>\n                                <p class=\"text-sm\">Use algebra to find unknowns</p>\n                            </li>\n                        </ol>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Practice Problems -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Practice Problems</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <ol class=\"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-4 text-gray-700\">\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-2\">Ladder Problem</p>\n                                <p>A ladder leans against a frictionless wall. Find the forces at both ends for equilibrium.</p>\n                            </li>\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-2\">Bridge Analysis</p>\n                                <p>A uniform bridge of weight W is supported at both ends. Find support forces when:</p>\n                                <ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm\">\n                                    <li>No load is present</li>\n                                    <li>A load P is placed at center</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </li>\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-2\">Hanging Sign</p>\n                                <p>A sign of mass M is supported by two cables at angles θ₁ and θ₂. Find tensions in the cables.</p>\n                            </li>\n                        </ol>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 to-indigo-100 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n        .content-card {\n            -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px);\n            backdrop-filter: blur(16px);\n            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);\n            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n            box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n        }"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}